Septuagint Study Bible: third-party material and licences (CLEAN-LICENCE PREVIEW, branch clean-license, not published)

Site licence: not decided yet. This build no longer uses the Rahlfs/CCAT data that required CC BY-NC-SA, so the LICENSE file
still needs a decision by the owner. Each part listed below keeps its own licence.

Greek text: L. C. L. Brenton's Greek text (The Septuagint Version of the Old Testament, with an English Translation, 1851;
  Vaticanus-based), eBible.org "grcbrent", public domain. The text is shown as eBible prints it; only punctuation is removed from the tappable words.
English: L. C. L. Brenton's translation (1851), eBible.org eng-Brenton, public domain. It is paired with the Greek above verse by verse,
  by the same reference. Where a clause clearly translates the neighbouring Greek verse, it is moved there automatically
  (build/tools/resegment.py); such verses are marked with ↕ in the app.
English: LXX2012: Septuagint in American English (2012), Michael Paul Johnson; updates dedicated to the public domain; eBible.org eng-lxx2012.

Dictionary forms (lemmas) and grammar tags: made automatically for this site. Forms Morpheus does not know are retried once
  with a regular spelling change (e.g. -οσαν to -ον; build/tools/prep_variants.py). The tags are the site's own output, not copied from a tagged text.
  - Morpheus morphological analyser (Perseus Project; perseids-tools/morpheus), Mozilla Public License 2.0. It was run on the build computer.
    Its analyses are used. Morpheus itself (code and stem library) is not included in the site.
  - STEPBible.org TAGNT (Translators Amalgamated Greek NT, Tyndale House, Cambridge), CC BY 4.0: NT word forms with their dictionary
    forms, used to choose between Morpheus analyses and for forms that Morpheus does not know.
  - STEPBible.org TBESG and TFLSJ headwords (CC BY 4.0) and Dodson headwords (public domain / CC0): used to spell dictionary forms and to
    match some names.
Dictionaries: STEPBible.org TBESG (Abbott-Smith) and TFLSJ (LSJ), Tyndale House, Cambridge, CC BY 4.0. The TBESG brief gloss is used as
  a plain meaning (label "STEP Bible") where Dodson has no entry.
Plain meanings: Dodson Greek-English Lexicon of the New Testament (Jeffrey Dodson; Ulrik Sandborg-Petersen conversion;
  github.com/biblicalhumanities/Dodson-Greek-Lexicon), public domain / CC0 1.0.
"Also in the NT" references: STEPBible TAGNT, CC BY 4.0. Words in the NA28 text, matched by dictionary form; only verse references and counts are stored.
Changes made to the dictionary text: spacing tidied; a leading "I"/"to" on verbs and "a/an/the" on nouns removed; Dodson's "am ..." written
  as "be ..."; STEP Bible's "base: specific" glosses reduced to the base; Dodson glosses with more than 3 senses or over 40 characters
  shortened to at most 3 of their own senses (full gloss under More); 19 headlines hand-written (build/tools/gloss_hand_plain.tsv, labelled
  "hand-written" on the card, original wording kept under More).
Brenton's wording (likely match): automatic word alignment built here from the Brenton Greek and Brenton English verse pairs only.
Font: Gentium Plus, SIL International, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL.txt).

SEPARATE CC BY-SA 4.0 LAYERS (ShareAlike applies to these files only):
- Wiktionary contributors, via kaikki.org Wiktextract (Tatu Ylonen), CC BY-SA 4.0:
  - data/etym/ : etymologies and derived words;
  - data/wk/   : links from about 1,170 word forms (0.2% of words) to their dictionary form, for forms the sources above do not cover.
    The app applies these links when it shows a chapter. The card says "from Wiktionary, CC BY-SA 4.0" on these words.

Not used in this build: Rahlfs 1935, CCAT/CATSS (University of Pennsylvania) morphology or lexicon, eliranwong/LXX-Rahlfs-1935, the Open
Scriptures LXX lexeme data, James Tauber's corrections of the CCAT tags, or SBLGNT and Douay-Rheims (the NT-quotation notes were removed,
because they described the Rahlfs wording).
